\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O word of pity, for our pardon pleading,
\par Breathed in the hour of loneliness and pain;
\par O voice, which, through the ages interceding,
\par Calls us to fellowship with God again.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O word of comfort, through 
\par the silence stealing,
\par As the dread act of sacrifice began,
\par O infinite compassion, still revealing,
\par The infinite forgiveness won for man.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O word of hope, to raise us nearer heaven,
\par When courage fails us, and when faith is dim;
\par The souls for whom Christ prays 
\par to Christ are given,
\par To find their pardon and their joy in Him.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O intercessor, who art ever living
\par To plead for dying souls that they may live,
\par Teach us to know our sin which 
\par needs forgiving,
\par Teach us to know the love which can forgive.
\par                                                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

